Z||000007||fropuff||02-27-2001||09:31 PM||||I don't know about you guys, but I really like the looks of these lights; the best ones, in my opinion.  I emailed RSM to ask a little information on them, and they did not say a frickin thing related to my question.  All I wanted to know is the type of lights they are.  All I wanted to do is replicate them, as those little bastards are $500!!  I'll keep my $500 and put it toward something useful.  If anyone can tell what kind of lights those are, I would greatly appreciate it.  Thanks a lot.<P>Here's the link: <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/light.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/light.jpg</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fropuff (edited 02-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jaei Sun||02-27-2001||09:54 PM||||How about these?<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mx5parts.co.uk/pix/L537.jpg">  <P>They're for a Mazda Miata but I bet they would work in a fiero if modified.  Now these are the BEST that I've seen!<P>I found a thread on a Miata board reguarding them:<P>"I have them on my '90. I don't have a moisture problem. They needed some work to fit them in, but I like'em."<P>Since you have to do a little work to make them fit in a miata (and that's what they're made for) might as well do some "work" to make them fit in a fiero.<P><A HREF="http://www.mx5parts.co.uk/pages/537.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mx5parts.co.uk/pages/537.htm</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Jaei Sun (edited 02-27-2001).]||||reg||1
